From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:44:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] radv: no layers is a complete answer to
 vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties

With an array, vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties returned
VK_ERROR_LAYER_NOT_PRESENT, though there being no layers is answered by
a count of 0 and VK_SUCCESS whatever was passed. The Khronos loader
answers the call itself, so this was never seen; but RADV is the PS4's
libvulkan.so.1, and there zink logged "ZINK: vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties
failed" on every start (it allocates an array for the 0 layers counted),
and a program that takes the error as fatal would not start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bb93U7uY5qVNuEcHDggEfE
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_instance.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_instance.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_instance.c
index eca90d3..8ad2aa5 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_instance.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_instance.c
@@ -435,13 +435,14 @@ radv_EnumerateInstanceVersion(uint32_t *pApiVersion)
 VKAPI_ATTR VkResult VKAPI_CALL
 radv_EnumerateInstanceLayerProperties(uint32_t *pPropertyCount, VkLayerProperties *pProperties)
 {
-   if (pProperties == NULL) {
-      *pPropertyCount = 0;
-      return VK_SUCCESS;
-   }
-
-   /* None supported at this time */
-   return vk_error(NULL, VK_ERROR_LAYER_NOT_PRESENT);
+   /* There are no layers: whether or not an array was passed, none is written
+    * and the count is 0, which is a complete answer (VK_SUCCESS). The Khronos
+    * loader answers this itself, but where RADV is libvulkan.so.1 (the PS4)
+    * its answer is the program's.
+    */
+   (void)pProperties;
+   *pPropertyCount = 0;
+   return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL
